; SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
;
; ScriptTarget — core.ScriptTarget, the members a ported branch names.
;
; Hand-ported, and declared up with the other constant tables since slice 140:
; both the SCANNER and the CHECKER read these, and a `define` read from a module
; declared LATER is a hard `unknown identifier` in operator position and is
; SILENTLY DROPPED along with the whole call as an argument. It lived in
; checker.scaly until the regular expression grammar became its second reader.

; ── ScriptTarget: the four values a ported branch reads ─────────────────────
;
; core.ScriptTarget, and the same rule as ModuleKind above: the members a reader
; actually names, with the reference's own numbers
; (internal/core/compileroptions.go), because a number is checkable and a name is
; not. The enum has fifteen.
;
; ★★★ ES2025 IS THE DERIVED DEFAULT AND IT IS THE **TOP** OF THE STANDARD RANGE,
; which is why every `languageVersion` guard in this port answers the same way and
; why none of them is dead code in the reference. `GetEmitScriptTarget()` falls
; through to `ScriptTargetLatestStandard` when Target is unset, and that is
; ES2025 = 12 — so a `>= ES2017` guard is TAKEN and a `<= ES2021` guard is not.
; See Checker.language_version.
; Slice 102's reader is the arithmetic arm's `**` fork on a BigInt pair, and it is
; the SECOND provably dead one: 12 < 3 is false, so TS2791 is never collected under
; this harness. It is written rather than dropped because the fork it guards decides
; nothing else — the arm answers bigintType either way — so the branch's absence and
; its presence are the same walk, and the reference's shape is the cheaper record.
; Slice 134's reader is getTypeFromArrayBindingPattern's `>= ES2015`, which the
; reference itself marks `// TODO: remove ScriptTargetES2015` — 12 >= 2, so the
; iterable branch is the live one and anyArrayType is unreachable from there.
define ScriptTargetES2015: int 2
define ScriptTargetES2016: int 3
define ScriptTargetES2017: int 4
; Slice 70's reader is checkGrammarBigIntLiteral's `< ES2020` guard, which is the
; fourth branch this list serves and the first that is provably DEAD: 12 < 7 is
; false, so a BigInt literal never collects TS2737 under this harness.
define ScriptTargetES2020: int 7
define ScriptTargetES2021: int 8
; Slice 74's reader is GetUseDefineForClassFields' fallthrough, and it is the
; threshold that makes checkClassForStaticPropertyNameConflicts inert: 12 >= 9.
define ScriptTargetES2022: int 9
define ScriptTargetES2025: int 12

; ── the four the REGULAR EXPRESSION grammar adds (slice 140) ────────────────
;
; None is the unset value `Scanner.languageVersion()` tests for, and Latest is
; what it answers there — the reference's ScriptTargetESNext, 99, which is above
; the standard range rather than inside it. ES2018 is the named-capturing-group
; threshold, ES2022/ES2024 two of the three flag-availability bounds (the third
; is ES2018 again).
;
; ★ ALL FOUR OF THOSE GUARDS ARE INERT UNDER THIS HARNESS and each says so where
; it stands: checkGrammarRegularExpressionLiteral sets the scanner's target from
; Checker.language_version, which is ES2025 = 12, and 12 is at or above every
; bound. They are written rather than dropped for the reason the ES2020 guard
; above is: the fork decides nothing else, so its presence and its absence are
; the same walk.
define ScriptTargetNone: int 0
define ScriptTargetES2018: int 5
; ── the two the driver chapter's option parser adds (slice 243): a case's
; `@target: es2019` / `es2023` — ★they were the only two missing, and a
; `return ScriptTargetES2019` of an UNDEFINED name compiles and answers 0
; (root CLAUDE.md), which made es2019 the DEFAULT target for a whole run
define ScriptTargetES2019: int 6
define ScriptTargetES2023: int 10
define ScriptTargetES2024: int 11
define ScriptTargetLatest: int 99

; printer/emitresolver.go TypeReferenceSerializationKind (slice 245) — in a module declared before the
; checker, because a constant of a LATER module read as a whole `return` is a silent 0
; (root CLAUDE.md); TypeFlags.scaly is GENERATED and lost them once (§3.5jr)
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindUnknown: int 0
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindTypeWithConstructSignatureAndValue: int 1
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindVoidNullableOrNeverType: int 2
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindNumberLikeType: int 3
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindBigIntLikeType: int 4
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindStringLikeType: int 5
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindBooleanType: int 6
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindArrayLikeType: int 7
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindESSymbolType: int 8
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindPromise: int 9
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindTypeWithCallSignature: int 10
define TypeReferenceSerializationKindObjectType: int 11


